                    "message": "why?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "JsonSchemas output has over 100 entries but not sorted (i.e. listed in the file system). \nChecking a schema in the list is not straightforward (e.g. Redfish Service validator report).\nAlthough it is not a functional issue (i.e. still can be done by sorting it by the reader), it would be much better if Redfish output is already sorted."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> Checking a schema in the list is not straightforward\n\nThis needs to be in your commit message.  There's no requirement that this list be sorted.  If the goal is that humans can read it easier, that's fine, but needs to be in the commit message.  As written this makes it sound like it's a spec violation to be out of order, which it's not."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the suggestion.\nI'll do."
                },
                {
